you need to install container runtime, kubeadm, kubectl, kubelet on all the nodes to begin setting up a cluster

## choose a container runtime
- containerd 
- cri-o
- docker-engine
install a desired container runtime on all the nodes.
### install docker engine on ubuntu manually
go to:<br>
https://download.docker.com/linux/ubuntu/dists//pool/stable/amd64/
then proceed by the information of your case: CODE_NAME > pool > stable > architecture of your cpu <br>
and download these packages:
- containerd.io_<version>_<arch>.deb
- docker-ce_<version>_<arch>.deb
- docker-ce-cli_<version>_<arch>.deb
- docker-buildx-plugin_<version>_<arch>.deb
- docker-compose-plugin_<version>_<arch>.deb

move them all in a dir and install them:<br>
`sudo dpkg -i *.deb`

test it:<br>
`sudo systemctl status docker`

